  "slug": "harmonic-generation-uv-1987",
  "summary": "Gold nano-pillar metasurfaces now reach UV and deep-UV harmonic generation, while plasmonic quantum-well SHG models add a formal treatment of the same platform class.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is nonlinear frequency conversion in engineered sub-wavelength structures. arxiv:2611.17037 reports experiments and full-vector simulations showing that resonant gold nano-pillar metasurfaces enhance second and third harmonic generation into the UV and deep-UV under ultrafast excitation. arxiv:2611.23943 offers a semi-analytical framework for second-harmonic generation in plasmonic metasurfaces with multiple quantum wells, addressing nonlinear current density, saturation, periodic SH boundary conditions, and the development of boundary conditions. arxiv:2611.24530 shares only the sub-wavelength grating design approach, using it to confine surface acoustic waves for a mid-infrared acousto-optic phase modulator at 460 MHz on GaAs/AlGaAs. What is new across the set is the experimental extension of resonant harmonic conversion into the UV regime and the formal modeling of metasurface SHG with quantum-well nonlinearities.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
